    "bug_category_descriptions": {
      "Input-triggered crashes": "Server-side crashes, assertions, or arithmetic faults (SIGFPE, OOB) triggered by malformed or edge-case client inputs such as empty/zero fields, non-finite floats, or oversized values. Probes single-node robustness to adversarial and corner-case requests.",
      "Concurrency hazards": "Data races, deadlocks, and livelocks arising from interleavings between client requests, background workers, and state transitions. Reproduction requires specific thread/goroutine scheduling.",
      "Replication & consistency violations": "Cross-replica divergence, lost updates, linearizability gaps, and silent data corruption on the leader-follower or log-replication path. Detectable only by cross-replica or invariant oracles.",
      "Protocol & recovery failures": "Defects in cluster-coordination protocols and recovery paths \u2014 leader election, membership and configuration change, snapshot/WAL replay, and RPC state-machine transitions \u2014 that surface after crashes, failovers, or other protocol edge cases.",
      "Resource & delivery anomalies": "Resource leaks, performance degradation, storage I/O-path misbehavior, and delivery/notification failures that degrade service availability or SLOs without crashing the server."
